Sara (not her real name) works in a bank in Abu Dhabi and sits Level I in August 2027. That gives her about nine months at 8 to 10 hours a week, which is enough for the 300 hours.

Her first timed test: above 70% on Ethics and Quantitative Methods, under 50% on Financial Statement Analysis and Fixed Income. A group class would take her through all ten topics at the same pace. Instead she:

- reads the curriculum on her own for the topics she already scores well on;
- books 10 hours of 1-on-1 coaching on FSA and Fixed Income: 10 × AED 150 = **AED 1,500**;
- takes one month of coaching before the exam for mock reviews: 30 hours for **AED 3,000**, which works out at AED 100 an hour.

Her total coaching cost is AED 4,500 for 40 hours, all of it on topics where she was losing marks. If her first test had been under 50% on most topics, a full group course or [monthly coaching](/courses/cfa-level-i) from the start would have made more sense.
